# Do Not Commit Generated Test-Run Artifacts

Several files are produced or mutated by running the agent (`main.py run`,
`main.py list`, `main.py health`, `main.py stress_test`). Do not sweep this
incidental churn into a feature commit.

## `_health.json` snapshots

- `tests/**/_health.json` files are tracked, but they are regenerated on most
  runs. A local run will frequently leave `tests/<category>/_health.json` shown
  as modified even when you changed nothing meaningful.
- Do NOT stage `_health.json` changes that are just run-generated churn. Only
  commit a `_health.json` update when you deliberately refreshed the snapshot
  and reviewed the diff (see commit `89d7666`, "drop stale payments health
  snapshot", where unintended snapshot churn was reverted in review).
- Before committing, discard incidental churn:
  `git checkout -- tests/<category>/_health.json`

## Output directories (never committed)

- `reports/` — stress/focused run logs. Git-ignored; never stage it.
- `**/_runs/*` and `runs_index/` — per-category run history. Git-ignored.

## When committing test work

- Stage explicit paths (the source, `steps.md`, `script.md`, `test.py`,
  `changelog.md`, `_category.yaml`). Avoid `git add -A`, which pulls in
  `_health.json` churn and stray output.
- `migration_mapping.md` and root `plan.md` are local planning artifacts and are
  git-ignored; keep them out of commits.
